=================
CI singles window
=================

. Single excitations S are selected in an energy window
  so that:

     |E_S| < tol_S,

  where E_S is the singles excitation energy calculated
  by Koopman's theorem i.e. orbital energy differences,

. Single excitation S is specified by:
  - I -> A where I < 1 are occupied MOs; 0 is the HOMO
  -        where A > 0 are virtual  MOs; 1 is the LUMO

. Improved virtual MO energies may be used, if requested,
  and if VMO canonicalisation was used in the SCF.

